{
  "_experiment": "FIX THE SECOND ONE-SIDED CLAMP: the `recovery` term (C45). 0 GPU-h.",
  "_evidence_class": "MEASURED (ours; artifact = these JSONs + pw_*.npz)",
  "_protocol": "PSEUDO-SIMULATION. Perturbed observation states are PRE-GENERATED on a bounded grid and the planner is evaluated ONCE from each. There is no sequential rollout, so deviation is CHOSEN, not accumulated, and cannot leave the validated envelope. Re-implemented from the published protocol (NAVSIM v2 / arXiv 2506.04218, CoRL 2025) on OUR data and OUR warp; no NAVSIM code or data is vendored.",
  "_estimator": "taniteval.ci.episode_cluster_bootstrap / paired form (B=2000, unit = val episode)",
  "_refused_estimator": "overlapping_holdout_se \u2014 it biases the POINT ESTIMATE as well as the interval",
  "_gate": "PANEL-WIDE. The per-arm gate is REFUSED, not offered.",
